I'm Kim Mills. My guest today is Dr. Michael Lynn, a professor of consumer behavior and marketing at the Peter and Stephanie Nolan School of Hotel Administration at Cornell University. He has studied tipping behavior for more than 30 years. His interest was first sparked when he paid his way through school by waiting tables and bartending. He's published more than 50 journal articles on tipping, and his work has been covered by dozens of mainstream media outlets, including the Wall Street Journal, The New York Times, NPR, the PBS News Hour, and CBS News. His new book published in February is called The Psychology of Tipping, Scientific Insights for Services, Customers, Workers, and Managers. Dr. Lynn, thank you for joining me today.
我是 Kim Mills。我今天的嘉宾是康奈尔大学彼得和斯蒂芬妮·诺兰酒店管理学院的消费者行为与营销学教授 Michael Lynn 博士。他研究小费行为已经超过 30 年了。他的兴趣最初是在他通过做服务员和调酒师来支付学费时被激发的。他发表了 50 多篇关于小费的学术论文，他的研究被数十家主流媒体报道，包括《华尔街日报》、《纽约时报》、NPR、PBS 新闻一小时和 CBS 新闻。他二月份出版的新书名为《小费心理学：为服务人员、顾客、工人和经理提供的科学见解》。Lynn 博士，感谢您今天加入我的节目。

