Oh, thank you for inviting me. It's my pleasure to be here. Let's start with the big picture. Why do people tip and when you ask people what motivates them, what do they say? When you ask people, the overwhelming majority response is that people say they tip to reward good service. It turns out that's not as big a factor as people think. When I stand outside of restaurants and interview customers about their dining experience, for example, I find that the customer's own rating of service quality explains about 4% of the differences in tips left by different dining parties. That's bigger than you would expect by chance.
哦，谢谢您的邀请。很高兴能来到这里。让我们从大局谈起。人们为什么给小费？当你问人们是什么激励他们时，他们会说什么？当你问人们时，绝大多数人的回答是他们给小费是为了奖励优质服务。事实证明，这并不是人们想象中那么大的因素。例如，当我站在餐馆外采访顾客关于他们的用餐体验时，我发现顾客自己对服务质量的评价仅能解释不同用餐群体所给小费差异的约 4%。这比你偶然预期的要大。

