feels different from seeing a tip jar on the counter? Does the screen actually help us determine how much to tip, or was it created to just push us to leave more? First off, the screen does typically contain one-touch options, which come across as defining social expectations and norms, whereas the tip dart doesn't have that. By the way, research shows that the more you ask for, the more you get.
