The larger the options, the more likely people are to opt out and say, I'm not going to tip at all, but the tips from those who do decide to tip are, are larger and the net effect on income is to increase income. And that's one of the reasons you see this escalation in the amounts people are asking for because it increases tip income. But it's not just those one touch options that are different. In a tip jar, if I don't tip, I simply refrain from putting money into the tip jar. It is a sin of omission. To leave no tip and these digital devices, I have to actively hit a button that says no tip. That's a sin of commission.
选项越大，人们越有可能选择退出，说“我根本不给小费”，但那些决定给小费的人给的金额更大，对收入的净影响是增加收入。这就是为什么你会看到人们要求的小费金额不断升级的原因之一，因为它增加了小费收入。但不仅仅是那些一键式选项不同。在小费罐里，如果我不给小费，我只是不往罐子里放钱。这是一种“不作为的罪”。而不给小费，在这些数字设备上，我必须主动点击一个写着“无小费”的按钮。这是一种“作为的罪”。

